WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:01.890
- [Reporter] In late May,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.130
three months after the US
imposed sanctions on Russian oil,

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.500
gasoline made from Russian
crude was delivered

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.080
to this terminal in New Jersey.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.220
It was later distributed

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.833
to gas stations across the East Coast.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.803
It came from this refinery in Italy.

00:00:19.855 --> 00:00:21.750
That's because of a US sanctions loophole

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.240
that allows banned Russian
crude to be refined

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.290
in a country outside of
Russia and sent to the US.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.100
We tracked ships, pieced together
months of commodity data,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.070
shipping documents, and satellite imagery

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.100
to reveal how Russia's second
largest oil and gas company,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.460
Lukoil, is sending Russian
oil refined in Italy

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.950
to companies like Exxon
in the United States

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.053
without violating sanctions.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.964
Our investigation shows

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:51.510
that Lukoil's ISAB refinery
in Syracuse, Sicily

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.270
represents one of the
most extreme examples

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:55.860
of this loophole.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.230
The vast majority of the
crude for this refinery

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.670
comes from Russia.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.950
It's then refined in Sicily,

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.410
after which it's considered Italian

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.660
thanks to a longstanding industry practice

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.970
that allows the origin of oil to change

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.503
based on where it's refined.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.350
The US launched sanctions against Russia

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.110
as punishment for invading
Ukraine in late February,

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.630
banning imports of Russian
oil and oil products

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.610
as well as blacklisting Russian oligarchs

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:23.634
and companies the US says
are close to President Putin.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:24.930
(soft tense music)

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.030
Unlike Russia's largest state-owned oil

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.423
and gas company, Rosneft,
Lukoil was not sanctioned.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.080
Lukoil still has a presence in the US

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.660
and distributes oil products to 11 states

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.410
according to the company's website.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.330
The only reason it can sell
Russian oil into the US

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.610
is because it stops at
the refinery in Sicily

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:45.723
on its way here.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.850
Lukoil's refinery in Sicily
is the second largest in Italy

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.460
and the fifth largest in Europe.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.920
Before the war, it brought
in and blended crude oil

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.140
from at least 15 different countries,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.140
with an average of 30% coming from Russia.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.110
Now, the overwhelming majority
of it comes from Russia

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.150
because European banks
stopped lending money

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.290
to the ISAB refinery after
Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:13.110
As a result, the Lukoil
refinery was no longer able

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.240
to buy crude from other countries.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.150
Since April, as much as
93% of its feed stock

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.130
is pure Russian crude.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.710
The rest is a Russian-Kazakh
blend or Kazakh,

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.593
according to data from
commodity tracking firm Vortexa.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.950
All of the crude came from Russian ports,

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.200
with the most coming from Primorsk.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.700
We see a shipment loading there

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.490
in this satellite image from late March.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.860
The vessel here is the SCF Baltica,

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.180
a tanker belonging to Russia's

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.940
largest state-owned shipping
company, Sovcomflot,

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.460
a company sanctioned by the US.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.070
Sovcomflot did not respond
to our request for comment.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.110
We see the same ship
again a few weeks later

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.753
delivering that oil to
the refinery in Sicily.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.800
It's this crucial stop that
eventually allows Lukoil

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.800
to sell this oil as gasoline
and other products to the US.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.480
A spokeswoman for the US
Department of the Treasury,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.640
which administers and enforces sanctions,

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.480
declined to comment, but US
sanctions state an exception

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.190
for any Russian origin good

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.990
that has been substantially transformed

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:14.613
into a foreign-made product.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.520
In general, substantial transformation

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.560
means that the oil has been changed

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.413
through processing or
manufacturing, such as refining.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.690
Refining is a process

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.213
in which crude is heated and distilled.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.690
While this process technically
transforms the crude

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.140
into a different product,
if the same raw ingredients

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.230
used in Lukoil's Sicily
refinery were brought to the US,

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.213
it would be a violation of sanctions.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.020
The refinery exported
almost five million barrels

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.930
of oil products to the US
since March of this year.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.903
Roughly 2.5 million of
those barrels were gasoline.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.560
According to the American
Petroleum Institute,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.510
that's enough to fill about seven million

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.790
automobile gas tanks.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.870
We traced shipments

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.880
delivered to at least
seven different buyers

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.940
in at least 13 different locations.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.590
Some of this was gasoline.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.330
While we can see where it was delivered,

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.660
shipping data doesn't
always identify the buyer.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.630
Data shows fuel, oil, and
gasoline were purchased

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.640
by Exxon and oil trading companies

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.163
such as Lukoil's own trading arm, Litasco.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.760
The most oil products
sent from Lukoil Sicily

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.580
to the US since March
went to Exxon's terminal

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.283
in Baytown, Texas, just outside Houston.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.690
Nearby, a terminal owned by
Magellan Midstream Partners,

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.690
a company that transports
and distributes oil products,

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.763
received the largest amount of gasoline.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.280
A spokesperson for Magellan said,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.930
although they received the shipment,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.430
they were not the buyer

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.263
and shipping data does not list one.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.240
Another gasoline shipment,
over 300,000 barrels,

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.030
arrived at this terminal in New Jersey.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.490
Shipping data indicates the
receiver for that delivery

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.440
was also Exxon.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.910
A spokeswoman from Exxon said

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.670
ExxonMobil is complying with all sanctions

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:02.070
and that deliveries it
received are certified products

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.393
of Italian origin.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.893
Lukoil did not respond to
multiple requests for comment.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.420
Though shipments like these
from Lukoil's Sicily refinery

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.720
may represent only a
fraction of US oil imports,

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.910
they reveal how difficult it is to track

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:21.150
and eliminate Russian oil
in the US supply chain.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.770
The Lukoil refinery in Sicily

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.960
will be forced to stop
importing Russian crude

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.080
and may have to close when
European sanctions banning it

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.943
come into effect on December 5th.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:34.950
In the meantime, at a number
of gas stations across the US,

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.890
Americans are filling up their
vehicles, paying for fuel

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.172
that, in part, adds to Russia's profits.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:43.089
(soft tense music)

